<title>CHINA: China completes 1996 tax collection.</title>
<headline>China completes 1996 tax collection.</headline>
<dateline>BEIJING 1996-12-27</dateline>
<text>
<p>China has completed its 1996 tax collection six days before the end of the year, the State Administration of Taxation said.</p>
<p>By December 25, China had collected 610 billion yuan ($75 billion) in industrial and commercial tax revenue, a 98-billion-yuan, or 19 percent, increase over 1995, state media on Friday quoted the administration as saying.</p>
<p>The figure was 1.2 percent higher than projected tax revenue for the year, it said.</p>
<p>It was the sixth successive year that China had reached its tax quota ahead of schedule, it said.</p>
</text>
